branch: feature/receive-blocking-path-length

why: channel-elementwise-wakeups closed with a count — no parks on
  either side — and the harness: okaySentinelElem 205.9 us against
  okaySentinelChunk 55.0 at the same 77-80 B per element. So the 3.7x
  is path length per call: a Handoff made per receiveBlocking, the scan's
  shared reads, the await. Candidates, measured one at a time on
  okaySentinelElem (-prof gc, 2 forks) with okaySentinelChunk as the
  control: (1) a per-thread Handoff reused across calls on JVM/Native
  (a thread blocks on at most one), (2) the scan's shared reads folded.
  Nothing that reads the producer's line. Laws: TestChannelLaws, TestHandoff,
  the cross channel suites; a Handoff reused must be reset before reuse
  and never observed by a late callback from a previous call.
